IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-insurable-employment`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), PART VII.1 (Benefits for self-employed persons), section 152.01:
-- the definitions of the Part, the amount of self-employed earnings for a year, and the reading rules of
-- subsections (3) to (5). Piece ei5, written by the piece agent ei5 (Sonnet 5.5).
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30;
-- nothing here claims to be verified against the official text.
--
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the Act's text alone; no point of view. The seat layer (ei5-seat.l4)
-- asks the questions from the position of the individual.
--
-- Every rule takes plain facts as its own GIVEN parameters (the stable binary rejects a GIVEN on a section).
-- A fact that the Regulations or another Part decide is a plain input with a comment
-- "out of range: <provision> (piece X)"; NOTES.md lists them under "Cross-references out of my ranges".
-- The Regulations are never quoted here: every src: line is a line of the Act's raw file.
-- Dates: the text of this section states no enactment, assent or commencement date (see NOTES.md).

§ `Part VII.1 -- Benefits for self-employed persons`

§§ `152.01 Interpretation -- definitions (subsection (1))`

-- "business" is an open list that carries one exclusion. A listed kind is JUST TRUE; an office or an
-- employment is JUST FALSE, because the definition says so; anything else is NOTHING, because the
-- definition does not say that something else is not a business ("undertaking of any kind whatever").
DECLARE `ei5 Kind of activity the definition of business lists` IS ONE OF
    `ei5 business - a profession`
    `ei5 business - a calling`
    `ei5 business - a trade`
    `ei5 business - a manufacture`
    `ei5 business - an undertaking of any kind whatever`
    `ei5 business - an adventure or concern in the nature of trade`
    `ei5 business - an office`
    `ei5 business - an employment`
    `ei5 business - something not on the list`

-- src:2117 | business includes a profession, calling, trade, manufacture or undertaking of any kind whatever, and includes an adventure or concern in the nature of trade but does not include an office or employment. (entreprise)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.01(1) "business" (src:2117)
GIVEN kind IS A `ei5 Kind of activity the definition of business lists`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.01(1) business includes` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `ei5 business - an office` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `ei5 business - an employment` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `ei5 business - something not on the list` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "balance-due day ... for a year": the day on which the premium for the year falls due (s 152.25).
-- "died after October in the year and before May in the immediately following year" is read by calendar
-- month: a death in November or December of the year, or in January to April of the next year.
-- A death on 31 October is therefore in "any other case" (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
-- "6 months after the day of death" uses `add months`, which clamps to the last day of the month.
-- src:2114 | balance-due day of a self-employed person for a year means
-- src:2115 | (a) if the person died after October in the year and before May in the immediately following year, the day that is 6 months after the day of death, and
-- src:2116 | (b) in any other case, April 30 in the immediately following year. (date d’exigibilité du solde)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.01(1) "balance-due day" (src:2114-2116)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the day of death` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 152.01(1) balance-due day of a self-employed person for a year` IS
    CONSIDER `the day of death`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `April 30 in the immediately following year`
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        IF `died after October in the year and before May in the immediately following year` d
        THEN `add months` d 6
        ELSE `April 30 in the immediately following year`
    WHERE
        `April 30 in the immediately following year` MEANS YMD (year PLUS 1) 4 30
        `died after October in the year and before May in the immediately following year` x MEANS
                (DATE_YEAR x EQUALS year AND DATE_MONTH x AT LEAST 11)
            OR  (DATE_YEAR x EQUALS (year PLUS 1) AND DATE_MONTH x AT MOST 4)

-- "disentitled means not entitled under sections 49, 50, 152.03, 152.15 or 152.2 or under the regulations".
-- Sections 152.03, 152.15 and 152.2 are in this Part: a caller passes the result of their rules.
-- src:2118 | disentitled means not entitled under sections 49, 50, 152.03, 152.15 or 152.2 or under the regulations. (inadmissible)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.01(1) "disentitled" (src:2118)
GIVEN `not entitled under section 49` IS A BOOLEAN                       -- out of range: section 49 (piece ei2)
      `not entitled under section 50` IS A BOOLEAN                       -- out of range: section 50 (piece ei2)
      `not entitled under section 152.03` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not entitled under section 152.15` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not entitled under section 152.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not entitled under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN                  -- out of range: the Regulations (pieces er1 to er6)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.01(1) disentitled` IF
        `not entitled under section 49`
    OR  `not entitled under section 50`
    OR  `not entitled under section 152.03`
    OR  `not entitled under section 152.15`
    OR  `not entitled under section 152.2`
    OR  `not entitled under the regulations`

-- "family member [Repealed, 2017, c. 20, s. 242]": nothing to encode (the Regulations, reg 1(3), piece er1,
-- define the term for ss 152.06, 152.061 and 152.062).

-- "initial claim for benefits means a claim made for the purpose of establishing a self-employed person's benefit period".
-- src:2120 | initial claim for benefits means a claim made for the purpose of establishing a self-employed person’s benefit period. (demande initiale de prestations)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.01(1) "initial claim for benefits" (src:2120)
GIVEN `it is a claim for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made by a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made for the purpose of establishing that person's benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.01(1) initial claim for benefits` IF
        `it is a claim for benefits`
    AND `it is made by a self-employed person`
    AND `it is made for the purpose of establishing that person's benefit period`

-- "qualifying period means the period described in section 152.08": see `s 152.08(1) the qualifying period of a
-- self-employed person` in ei5-qualifying.
-- "waiting period means the one week of the benefit period described in section 152.15": see
-- `s 152.15 the waiting period of a self-employed person, in weeks` in ei5-payment.

-- "self-employed person means an individual who (a) is or was engaged in a business; or (b) is employed but does
-- not have insurable employment by reason of paragraph 5(2)(b)."
-- Paragraph (b): the keel rule for s 5(2)(b) says whether the employment is the employment of a person by a
-- corporation they control (more than 40% of the voting shares); "by reason of" is read as: the employment would
-- be insurable employment but for that paragraph (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2122 | self-employed person means an individual who
-- src:2123 | (a) is or was engaged in a business; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.01(1) "self-employed person" paragraph (a) (src:2122-2123)
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is or was engaged in a business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.01(1) self-employed person, paragraph (a)` IF
        `is an individual`
    AND `is or was engaged in a business`

-- src:2122 | self-employed person means an individual who
-- src:2124 | (b) is employed but does not have insurable employment by reason of paragraph 5(2)(b).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.01(1) "self-employed person" paragraph (b) (src:2122) (src:2124)
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment would be insurable employment but for paragraph 5(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the portion of the voting shares of the corporation that the person controls` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.01(1) self-employed person, paragraph (b)` IF
        `is an individual`
    AND `is employed`
    AND `the employment would be insurable employment but for paragraph 5(2)(b)`
    AND `s 5(2)(b) employment of a person by a corporation they control` `the employer is a corporation` `the portion of the voting shares of the corporation that the person controls`

-- The closing sentence takes out of the definition the individuals to whom regulations made under Part VIII
-- (fishing) apply and the individuals whose employment is included in insurable employment by a regulation made
-- under paragraph 5(4)(c).
-- src:2122 | self-employed person means an individual who
-- src:2123 | (a) is or was engaged in a business; or
-- src:2124 | (b) is employed but does not have insurable employment by reason of paragraph 5(2)(b).
-- src:2125 | However, individuals to whom regulations made under Part VIII apply, and individuals whose employment is included in insurable employment by a regulation made under paragraph 5(4)(c), are not included in this definition. (travailleur indépendant)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.01(1) "self-employed person" (src:2122-2125)
GIVEN `paragraph (a) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations made under Part VIII apply to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: Part VIII (piece ei4)
      `the individual's employment is included in insurable employment by a regulation made under paragraph 5(4)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: s 5(4)(c), reg 6 (piece er1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.01(1) self-employed person` IF
        (`paragraph (a) applies` OR `paragraph (b) applies`)
    AND NOT (`regulations made under Part VIII apply to the individual`)
    AND NOT (`the individual's employment is included in insurable employment by a regulation made under paragraph 5(4)(c)`)

§§ `152.01 Interpretation -- the amount of self-employed earnings for a year (subsections (2) and (3))`

-- One business of the year, as the Income Tax Act computes it. The Act speaks of "their businesses"; a caller
-- passes one record per business. The figure "computed without reference to paragraph 81(1)(a)" is only read
-- for the income of an Indian on a reserve (subsection (3)).
DECLARE `ei5 Business of the year` HAS
    `ei5 income of the business for the year, computed under the Income Tax Act` IS A NUMBER                                                   -- out of range: the Income Tax Act
    `ei5 income of the business for the year, computed without reference to paragraph 81(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act` IS A NUMBER             -- out of range: the Income Tax Act
    `ei5 the income is that of an Indian, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act, on a reserve, as defined in that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the Indian Act
    `ei5 gross revenue of the business for the year` IS A NUMBER
    `ei5 rent from land or buildings in that gross revenue` IS A NUMBER

-- src:2138 | (3) For the purpose of clause (2)(a)(i)(A), the income of an Indian, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act, on a reserve, as defined in that subsection, is to be calculated without reference to paragraph 81(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.01(3) (src:2138)
GIVEN business IS A `ei5 Business of the year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.01(3) the income of a business for clause (2)(a)(i)(A)` IS
    IF business's `ei5 the income is that of an Indian, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act, on a reserve, as defined in that subsection`
    THEN business's `ei5 income of the business for the year, computed without reference to paragraph 81(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act`
    ELSE business's `ei5 income of the business for the year, computed under the Income Tax Act`

-- "a business more than fifty per cent of the gross revenue of which consisted of rent from land or buildings":
-- strictly more than half; exactly half does not take the business out.
-- src:2131 | (A) their income for the year, computed under the Income Tax Act, from their businesses, other than a business more than fifty per cent of the gross revenue of which consisted of rent from land or buildings,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.01(2)(a)(i)(A) (src:2131)
GIVEN business IS A `ei5 Business of the year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.01(2)(a)(i)(A) a business more than fifty per cent of the gross revenue of which consisted of rent from land or buildings` IF
    business's `ei5 rent from land or buildings in that gross revenue` GREATER THAN business's `ei5 gross revenue of the business for the year` TIMES 50%

-- src:2131 | (A) their income for the year, computed under the Income Tax Act, from their businesses, other than a business more than fifty per cent of the gross revenue of which consisted of rent from land or buildings,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.01(2)(a)(i)(A) (src:2131)
GIVEN businesses IS A LIST OF `ei5 Business of the year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.01(2)(a)(i)(A) their income for the year from their businesses, other than a rental business` IS
    sum (map (GIVEN b YIELD `s 152.01(3) the income of a business for clause (2)(a)(i)(A)` b)
             (filter (GIVEN b YIELD NOT (`s 152.01(2)(a)(i)(A) a business more than fifty per cent of the gross revenue of which consisted of rent from land or buildings` b)) businesses))

-- src:2130 | (i) an amount equal to
-- src:2131 | (A) their income for the year, computed under the Income Tax Act, from their businesses, other than a business more than fifty per cent of the gross revenue of which consisted of rent from land or buildings,
-- src:2132 | minus
-- src:2133 | (B) all losses, computed under the Income Tax Act, sustained by the self-employed person in the year in carrying on the businesses they are engaged in, and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.01(2)(a)(i) (src:2130-2133)
GIVEN businesses IS A LIST OF `ei5 Business of the year`
      `all losses, computed under the Income Tax Act, sustained in the year in carrying on the businesses they are engaged in` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: the Income Tax Act
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.01(2)(a)(i) the amount equal to their business income less their business losses` IS
    `s 152.01(2)(a)(i)(A) their income for the year from their businesses, other than a rental business` businesses
        MINUS `all losses, computed under the Income Tax Act, sustained in the year in carrying on the businesses they are engaged in`

-- src:2134 | (ii) their income for the year from employment described in paragraph 5(6)(c) that has been excluded from insurable employment by a regulation made under subsection 5(6), as that income is computed under the Income Tax Act;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.01(2)(a)(ii) (src:2134)
GIVEN `their income for the year from employment described in paragraph 5(6)(c) that has been excluded from insurable employment by a regulation made under subsection 5(6), as computed under the Income Tax Act` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: s 5(6)(c), regs 7 and 8 (piece er1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.01(2)(a)(ii) their income for the year from employment excluded by a regulation under paragraph 5(6)(c)` IS
    `their income for the year from employment described in paragraph 5(6)(c) that has been excluded from insurable employment by a regulation made under subsection 5(6), as computed under the Income Tax Act`

-- src:2129 | (a) in the case of a self-employed person who is an individual referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition self-employed person in subsection (1), the amount that is the aggregate of
-- src:2130 | (i) an amount equal to
-- src:2131 | (A) their income for the year, computed under the Income Tax Act, from their businesses, other than a business more than fifty per cent of the gross revenue of which consisted of rent from land or buildings,
-- src:2132 | minus
-- src:2133 | (B) all losses, computed under the Income Tax Act, sustained by the self-employed person in the year in carrying on the businesses they are engaged in, and
-- src:2134 | (ii) their income for the year from employment described in paragraph 5(6)(c) that has been excluded from insurable employment by a regulation made under subsection 5(6), as that income is computed under the Income Tax Act;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.01(2)(a) (src:2129-2134)
GIVEN businesses IS A LIST OF `ei5 Business of the year`
      losses IS A NUMBER
      `income from employment excluded under paragraph 5(6)(c)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.01(2)(a) the self-employed earnings of an individual referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition` IS
    `s 152.01(2)(a)(i) the amount equal to their business income less their business losses` businesses losses
        PLUS `s 152.01(2)(a)(ii) their income for the year from employment excluded by a regulation under paragraph 5(6)(c)` `income from employment excluded under paragraph 5(6)(c)`

-- src:2135 | (b) in the case of a self-employed person who is an individual referred to in paragraph (b) of the definition self-employed person in subsection (1), the amount that would have been the person’s insurable earnings for the year had the person’s employment not been excluded from insurable employment; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.01(2)(b) (src:2135)
GIVEN `the person's insurable earnings for the year had the employment not been excluded from insurable employment` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: Part IV, s 5(2)(b) (piece ei3)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.01(2)(b) the self-employed earnings of an individual referred to in paragraph (b) of the definition` IS
    `the person's insurable earnings for the year had the employment not been excluded from insurable employment`

-- Subsection (2) says nothing about a person who is in neither paragraph: that case is not a self-employed person
-- at all, so the rule answers NOTHING (not covered) rather than 0.
-- Nor does it say that a negative result (losses above income) is raised to zero: it is not (fork F3).
-- src:2128 | (2) For the purpose of this Part, the amount of the self-employed earnings of a self-employed person for a year is,
-- src:2129 | (a) in the case of a self-employed person who is an individual referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition self-employed person in subsection (1), the amount that is the aggregate of
-- src:2130 | (i) an amount equal to
-- src:2131 | (A) their income for the year, computed under the Income Tax Act, from their businesses, other than a business more than fifty per cent of the gross revenue of which consisted of rent from land or buildings,
-- src:2132 | minus
-- src:2133 | (B) all losses, computed under the Income Tax Act, sustained by the self-employed person in the year in carrying on the businesses they are engaged in, and
-- src:2134 | (ii) their income for the year from employment described in paragraph 5(6)(c) that has been excluded from insurable employment by a regulation made under subsection 5(6), as that income is computed under the Income Tax Act;
-- src:2135 | (b) in the case of a self-employed person who is an individual referred to in paragraph (b) of the definition self-employed person in subsection (1), the amount that would have been the person’s insurable earnings for the year had the person’s employment not been excluded from insurable employment; and
-- src:2136 | (c) in the case of a self-employed person who is an individual referred to in both paragraphs (a) and (b), the amount that is the aggregate of the amounts referred to in both those paragraphs.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.01(2) (src:2128-2136)
GIVEN `referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `referred to in paragraph (b) of the definition self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount under paragraph (a)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount under paragraph (b)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.01(2) the amount of the self-employed earnings of a self-employed person for a year` IS
    BRANCH IF `referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition self-employed person` AND `referred to in paragraph (b) of the definition self-employed person`
                THEN JUST (`the amount under paragraph (a)` PLUS `the amount under paragraph (b)`)
           IF `referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition self-employed person`
                THEN JUST `the amount under paragraph (a)`
           IF `referred to in paragraph (b) of the definition self-employed person`
                THEN JUST `the amount under paragraph (b)`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `152.01 Interpretation -- week of unemployment and rounding (subsections (4) and (5))`

-- "a week of unemployment for a self-employed person is a week of unemployment as defined or determined in
-- accordance with the regulations": reg 30.1 for Part VII.1 (piece er2); a caller passes the result.
-- src:2140 | (4) For the purpose of this Part, a week of unemployment for a self-employed person is a week of unemployment as defined or determined in accordance with the regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.01(4) (src:2140)
GIVEN `the week is a week of unemployment as defined or determined in accordance with the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: regs 30.1 and 30.2 (piece er2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.01(4) week of unemployment for a self-employed person` IF
    `the week is a week of unemployment as defined or determined in accordance with the regulations`

-- Subsection (5), rounding to the nearest dollar, the higher dollar when equidistant: the keel rule
-- `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (eia-core) states it for this Part too; ss 152.16
-- and 152.17 call it and say so in their own comments.
